otentially combine with T3 and T5 to form a Chow? But T3 is used in across player's meld and my meld already used T1-T3, so unlikely. Bamboo tiles: B2 pair, B4, B6, B7, B8 are consecutive? B4, B6, B7, B8 are not fully consecutive; B4-B6 gap, B6-B7-B8 consecutive. So I have potential Chow B6-B7-B8 if I draw B5 or B9? Actually B6,B7,B8 is a Chow itself, but I have only one of each, so need another B6 or B7 or B8 to form a pair or meld. B2 pair is good for potential Pung or pair.  \n\nReason: Discarding T5 seems safe because I already have a Chow containing T5, and T5 is a middle tile not highly valuable for scoring patterns. Discarding T4 is also safe but T4 could potentially be used with B4 for mixed chow? Not really. Bamboo tiles have more potential since many are left and I have a sequence forming. I should keep Bamboo suit to aim for Half Flush (Bamboo + honors) or All Types if I pick up honors later. Also, discarding T5 reduces redundancy.  \n\nAnswer: Play T5"}
